IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc-definitions`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 9, RULES 20 TO 25: production, experts, independent witnesses and counsel, pre-trial examination,
-- directions for trial.  Part roc2, layer 1.  How to read a result: see roc2-order-9a.l4 and NOTES.md
-- ("Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (roc2)").  Every answer is subject to O 3 r 2(1) (roc1).

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 9, Rules 20 and 21 -- production of documents; expert evidence and assessors`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:937 | 20. The Court may order the production of documents in accordance with Order 11.
@ref O 9 r 20 (src:937)
GIVEN `the order is in accordance with Order 11` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 20 the Court may order the production of documents` MEANS
    IF `the order is in accordance with Order 11`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in accordance with Order 11" [marginal-b]

-- src:939 | 21. —(1) The parties are to inform the Court during the case conference if they intend to rely on expert evidence. (2) If one or more parties intend to rely on expert evidence, the Court must consider the matters set out in Order 12.
@ref O 9 r 21(1) (src:939)
GIVEN `the parties intend to rely on expert evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 21(1) the parties are to inform the Court during the case conference` MEANS
    IF `the parties intend to rely on expert evidence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if they intend to rely on expert evidence" [marginal-a]

-- src:939 | 21. —(1) The parties are to inform the Court during the case conference if they intend to rely on expert evidence. (2) If one or more parties intend to rely on expert evidence, the Court must consider the matters set out in Order 12.
@ref O 9 r 21(1) (src:939)
GIVEN `the parties inform the Court during the case conference` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 21(1) the parties have informed the Court as required` MEANS
    IF `the parties inform the Court during the case conference`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are to inform the Court during the case conference" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- src:939 | 21. —(1) The parties are to inform the Court during the case conference if they intend to rely on expert evidence. (2) If one or more parties intend to rely on expert evidence, the Court must consider the matters set out in Order 12.
@ref O 9 r 21(2) (src:939)
GIVEN `one or more parties intend to rely on expert evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 21(2) the Court must consider the matters set out in Order 12` MEANS
    IF `one or more parties intend to rely on expert evidence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If one or more parties intend to rely on expert evidence" [marginal-a]

DECLARE `o 9 r 21(3) a thing the Court may do about assessors` IS ONE OF
    `o 9 r 21(3) appoint one or more assessors`
    `o 9 r 21(3) give directions on the role of the assessors`
    `o 9 r 21(3) give directions on the remuneration of the assessors`

-- src:940 | (3) The Court may appoint one or more assessors upon application by any party or on its own accord and give directions on the role and the remuneration of the assessors.
@ref O 9 r 21(3) (src:940)
GIVEN thing IS A `o 9 r 21(3) a thing the Court may do about assessors`
      `a party applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court acts on its own accord` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 21(3) the Court may do this` MEANS
    IF `a party applies` OR `the Court acts on its own accord`
    THEN
        CONSIDER thing
        WHEN `o 9 r 21(3) appoint one or more assessors` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 9 r 21(3) give directions on the role of the assessors` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 9 r 21(3) give directions on the remuneration of the assessors` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "upon application by any party or on its own accord" (an "upon" read as "where", ruling of 2026-11-05) [marginal-a]

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 9, Rules 22 and 23 -- independent witnesses, interested non-parties, independent counsel`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:942 | 22. —(1) The Court may order, on its own accord, a person not named as a witness for any party to give evidence orally or by way of affidavit as an independent witness. (2) The Court may give directions for the cross‑examination of an independent witness.
@ref O 9 r 22(1) (src:942)
GIVEN `the Court acts on its own accord` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is not named as a witness for any party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 22(1) the Court may order the person to give evidence orally or by affidavit as an independent witness` MEANS
    IF `the Court acts on its own accord` AND `the person is not named as a witness for any party`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on its own accord, a person not named as a witness for any party" [marginal-b]

-- src:942 | 22. —(1) The Court may order, on its own accord, a person not named as a witness for any party to give evidence orally or by way of affidavit as an independent witness. (2) The Court may give directions for the cross‑examination of an independent witness.
@ref O 9 r 22(2) (src:942)
GIVEN `the person is an independent witness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 22(2) the Court may give directions for the cross-examination of the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is an independent witness`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an independent witness"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:943 | (3) The Court may invite any natural person or entity who has an interest or is able to assist in the issues in the case to give the person’s or entity’s views in writing on specific issues.
@ref O 9 r 22(3) (src:943)
GIVEN `the person is a natural person or entity who has an interest or is able to assist in the issues in the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 22(3) the Court may invite the person to give views in writing on specific issues` MEANS
    IF `the person is a natural person or entity who has an interest or is able to assist in the issues in the case`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any natural person or entity who has an interest or is able to assist in the issues in the case"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

DECLARE `o 9 r 22(4) a thing the interested person or entity might be required to do` IS ONE OF
    `o 9 r 22(4) be cross-examined`
    `o 9 r 22(4) attend the hearing`

-- src:944 | (4) The interested person or entity is not subject to cross‑examination and need not attend the hearing.
@ref O 9 r 22(4) (src:944)
GIVEN `the person is an interested person or entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      thing IS A `o 9 r 22(4) a thing the interested person or entity might be required to do`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 22(4) the interested person or entity is required to do this` MEANS
    IF `the person is an interested person or entity`
    THEN
        CONSIDER thing
        WHEN `o 9 r 22(4) be cross-examined` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not subject to cross-examination" (flat negative, ruling N2)
        WHEN `o 9 r 22(4) attend the hearing` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "need not attend the hearing" (flat negative, ruling N2)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The interested person or entity"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:945 | (5) The Court may order one or more of the parties to pay for the reasonable expenses incurred by an independent witness or an interested person or entity.
@ref O 9 r 22(5) (src:945)
GIVEN `the expenses were incurred by an independent witness or an interested person or entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expenses are reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 22(5) the Court may order one or more of the parties to pay the expenses` MEANS
    IF `the expenses were incurred by an independent witness or an interested person or entity` AND `the expenses are reasonable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the reasonable expenses incurred by an independent witness or an interested person or entity" [marginal-b]

-- src:947 | 23. —(1) The Court may, on its own accord, appoint one or more independent counsel (previously called the “amicus curiae”) to assist the Court in any matter on specific issues of law. (2) An independent counsel may be — ( a )
@ref O 9 r 23(1) (src:947)
GIVEN `the Court acts on its own accord` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the independent counsel is to assist the Court in a matter on specific issues of law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 23(1) the Court may appoint one or more independent counsel` MEANS
    IF `the Court acts on its own accord` AND `the independent counsel is to assist the Court in a matter on specific issues of law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on its own accord" ... "to assist the Court in any matter on specific issues of law" [marginal-b]

-- "independent counsel" (previously called the "amicus curiae") is a term defined in paragraph (1); who may be one is paragraph (2).
DECLARE `o 9 r 23(2) a kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `o 9 r 23(2)(a) a solicitor`
    `o 9 r 23(2)(b) an academic involved in the teaching of law at present or in the past`
    `o 9 r 23(2)(c) a person who has special knowledge or experience in any area of law`
    `o 9 r 23(2) any other person`

-- src:947 | 23. —(1) The Court may, on its own accord, appoint one or more independent counsel (previously called the “amicus curiae”) to assist the Court in any matter on specific issues of law. (2) An independent counsel may be — ( a )
-- src:948 | a solicitor;
-- src:949 | ( b )
-- src:950 | an academic involved in the teaching of law at present or in the past; or
-- src:951 | ( c )
-- src:952 | a person who has special knowledge or experience in any area of law.
@ref O 9 r 23(2) (src:947-952)
GIVEN person IS A `o 9 r 23(2) a kind of person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 23(2) the person may be an independent counsel` MEANS
    CONSIDER person
    WHEN `o 9 r 23(2)(a) a solicitor` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 9 r 23(2)(b) an academic involved in the teaching of law at present or in the past` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 9 r 23(2)(c) a person who has special knowledge or experience in any area of law` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 9 r 23(2) any other person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "An independent counsel may be" (a), (b) or (c); the text does not say that no one else may be

DECLARE `o 9 r 23(3) a matter on which the Court must give directions` IS ONE OF
    `o 9 r 23(3)(a) the specific issues of law to be addressed by the independent counsel`
    `o 9 r 23(3)(b) the filing and service of written submissions by the independent counsel and the parties`
    `o 9 r 23(3)(c) the independent counsel's attendance in Court to make oral submissions`

-- src:953 | (3) The Court must give directions to the independent counsel on — ( a )
-- src:954 | the specific issues of law to be addressed by the independent counsel;
-- src:955 | ( b )
-- src:956 | the filing and service of written submissions by the independent counsel and the parties; and
-- src:957 | ( c )
-- src:958 | the independent counsel’s attendance in Court to make oral submissions.
@ref O 9 r 23(3) (src:953-958)
GIVEN `an independent counsel has been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `o 9 r 23(3) a matter on which the Court must give directions`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 23(3) the Court must give directions to the independent counsel on this matter` MEANS
    IF `an independent counsel has been appointed`
    THEN
        CONSIDER matter
        WHEN `o 9 r 23(3)(a) the specific issues of law to be addressed by the independent counsel` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 9 r 23(3)(b) the filing and service of written submissions by the independent counsel and the parties` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 9 r 23(3)(c) the independent counsel's attendance in Court to make oral submissions` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the independent counsel"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 9, Rule 24 -- pre-trial examination`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:960 | 24. —(1) Where it is necessary in the interests of justice to record the evidence of any witness in or out of Singapore before a trial, a party may apply to the Court to make an order for pre‑trial examination. (2) The party who applies for an order for pre‑trial examination must file an affidavit showing that — ( a )
@ref O 9 r 24(1) (src:960)
GIVEN `it is necessary in the interests of justice to record the evidence of a witness in or out of Singapore before a trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 24(1) a party may apply to the Court for an order for pre-trial examination` MEANS
    IF `it is necessary in the interests of justice to record the evidence of a witness in or out of Singapore before a trial`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where it is necessary in the interests of justice to record the evidence of any witness in or out of Singapore before a trial" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

-- src:960 | 24. —(1) Where it is necessary in the interests of justice to record the evidence of any witness in or out of Singapore before a trial, a party may apply to the Court to make an order for pre‑trial examination. (2) The party who applies for an order for pre‑trial examination must file an affidavit showing that — ( a )
-- src:961 | the witness’ evidence is necessary for the party’s case;
-- src:962 | ( b )
-- src:963 | the other parties do not agree that the evidence of that witness be given in an affidavit without cross‑examination; and
-- src:964 | ( c )
-- src:965 | the witness will not be able or willing to attend the trial or to give evidence by live video or live television link, or the witness’ age or health makes it likely that he or she will pass away before or become incapable of testifying at the trial.
@ref O 9 r 24(2) (src:960-965)
GIVEN `the witness' evidence is necessary for the party's case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other parties do not agree that the evidence of that witness be given in an affidavit without cross-examination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the witness will not be able or willing to attend the trial or to give evidence by live video or live television link` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the witness' age or health makes it likely that he or she will pass away before or become incapable of testifying at the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 24(2) the affidavit shows what paragraph (2) requires` MEANS
    IF `the witness' evidence is necessary for the party's case` AND `the other parties do not agree that the evidence of that witness be given in an affidavit without cross-examination` AND (`the witness will not be able or willing to attend the trial or to give evidence by live video or live television link` OR `the witness' age or health makes it likely that he or she will pass away before or become incapable of testifying at the trial`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must file an affidavit showing that" (a), (b) and (c) (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- src:966 | (3) If the pre‑trial examination is to be conducted outside Singapore, the affidavit must also state — ( a )
-- src:967 | the place where the pre‑trial examination is to be conducted;
-- src:968 | ( b )
-- src:969 | that the law of that place allows the pre‑trial examination to be conducted in that place;
-- src:970 | ( c )
-- src:971 | the particulars and remuneration of the examiner who will be conducting the pre‑trial examination; and
-- src:972 | ( d )
-- src:973 | the rules that will apply to the pre‑trial examination.
@ref O 9 r 24(3) (src:966-973)
GIVEN `the pre-trial examination is to be conducted outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 24(3) the affidavit must also state the matters in paragraph (3)` MEANS
    IF `the pre-trial examination is to be conducted outside Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the pre-trial examination is to be conducted outside Singapore" [marginal-a]

-- src:966 | (3) If the pre‑trial examination is to be conducted outside Singapore, the affidavit must also state — ( a )
-- src:967 | the place where the pre‑trial examination is to be conducted;
-- src:968 | ( b )
-- src:969 | that the law of that place allows the pre‑trial examination to be conducted in that place;
-- src:970 | ( c )
-- src:971 | the particulars and remuneration of the examiner who will be conducting the pre‑trial examination; and
-- src:972 | ( d )
-- src:973 | the rules that will apply to the pre‑trial examination.
@ref O 9 r 24(3) (src:966-973)
GIVEN `the affidavit states the place where the pre-trial examination is to be conducted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states that the law of that place allows the pre-trial examination to be conducted in that place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states the particulars and remuneration of the examiner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavit states the rules that will apply to the pre-trial examination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 24(3) the affidavit states the matters in paragraph (3)` MEANS
    IF `the affidavit states the place where the pre-trial examination is to be conducted` AND `the affidavit states that the law of that place allows the pre-trial examination to be conducted in that place` AND `the affidavit states the particulars and remuneration of the examiner` AND `the affidavit states the rules that will apply to the pre-trial examination`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the affidavit must also state" (a), (b), (c) and (d) (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- src:974 | (4) If the law of the place for the pre‑trial examination outside of Singapore requires the issue of a letter of request to the relevant authorities for the evidence of the person in that jurisdiction to be taken, the party who applies for the order may include a request for the issue of a letter of request and such application can only be made in the General Division even if the proceedings are commenced in the State Courts.
@ref O 9 r 24(4) (src:974)
GIVEN `the law of the place for the pre-trial examination outside Singapore requires the issue of a letter of request` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 24(4) the party may include a request for the issue of a letter of request` MEANS
    IF `the law of the place for the pre-trial examination outside Singapore requires the issue of a letter of request`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the law of the place for the pre-trial examination outside of Singapore requires the issue of a letter of request" [marginal-a]

-- src:974 | (4) If the law of the place for the pre‑trial examination outside of Singapore requires the issue of a letter of request to the relevant authorities for the evidence of the person in that jurisdiction to be taken, the party who applies for the order may include a request for the issue of a letter of request and such application can only be made in the General Division even if the proceedings are commenced in the State Courts.
@ref O 9 r 24(4) (src:974)
GIVEN `the application includes a request for the issue of a letter of request` IS A BOOLEAN
      level IS A `Court level`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 24(4) the application for a letter of request may be made in this court` MEANS
    IF `the application includes a request for the issue of a letter of request`
    THEN
        IF level EQUALS `General Division`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "such application can only be made in the General Division even if the proceedings are commenced in the State Courts" (a list closed with "only")
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such application"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:975 | (5) For the purposes of paragraph (4), the party obtaining the order must prepare and file in the Registry — ( a )
-- src:976 | the letter of request which must be — (i)
-- src:977 | in a case where the jurisdiction in which the evidence is to be taken is a jurisdiction to which the Hague Evidence Convention applies — in the current version of the applicable Recommended Model Form; or
-- src:978 | (ii)
-- src:979 | in any other case — in Form 17,
-- src:980 | with such variations and in compliance with such requirements as may be required by the jurisdiction in which the evidence is to be taken or by the order; and
@ref O 9 r 24(5)(a) (src:975-980)
GIVEN `the Hague Evidence Convention applies to the jurisdiction in which the evidence is to be taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter of request is in the current version of the applicable Recommended Model Form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter of request is in Form 17` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 24(5)(a) the letter of request is in the form required` MEANS
    IF `the Hague Evidence Convention applies to the jurisdiction in which the evidence is to be taken`
    THEN
        IF `the letter of request is in the current version of the applicable Recommended Model Form`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the letter of request which must be ... in the current version of the applicable Recommended Model Form" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]
    ELSE
        IF `the letter of request is in Form 17`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any other case — in Form 17" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- src:981 | ( b )
-- src:982 | an undertaking in Form 18 signed by the party or the party’s solicitor to be responsible personally for all expenses incurred by an issuing authority or a transmitting authority in respect of the letter of request and, on receiving due notification of the amount of those expenses, to pay that amount to the issuing authority or transmitting authority and to produce a receipt for the payment to the proper officer of the Registry.
@ref O 9 r 24(5)(b) (src:981-982)
GIVEN `an undertaking in Form 18 is prepared and filed in the Registry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is signed by the party or the party's solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 24(5)(b) the undertaking is as required` MEANS
    IF `an undertaking in Form 18 is prepared and filed in the Registry` AND `it is signed by the party or the party's solicitor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must prepare and file in the Registry ... an undertaking in Form 18 signed by the party or the party's solicitor" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]

-- src:983 | (6) A pre‑trial examination in Singapore must be before a Judge or the Registrar and must be conducted according to the rules governing trials.
@ref O 9 r 24(6) (src:983)
GIVEN `the pre-trial examination is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is before a Judge or the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is conducted according to the rules governing trials` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 24(6) the pre-trial examination in Singapore is conducted as required` MEANS
    IF `the pre-trial examination is in Singapore`
    THEN
        IF `it is before a Judge or the Registrar` AND `it is conducted according to the rules governing trials`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be before a Judge or the Registrar and must be conducted according to the rules governing trials" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A pre-trial examination in Singapore"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:984 | (7) Where an order for pre‑trial examination in Singapore has been made, the attendance of the witness before the examiner in Singapore and the production by the witness of any document at the examination may be enforced by an order to attend court and an order to produce documents in like manner as the attendance of a witness and the production by a witness of a document at a trial may be enforced.
@ref O 9 r 24(7) (src:984)
GIVEN `an order for pre-trial examination in Singapore has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 24(7) the attendance of the witness and the production of documents may be enforced by an order to attend court and an order to produce documents` MEANS
    IF `an order for pre-trial examination in Singapore has been made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an order for pre-trial examination in Singapore has been made" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

-- src:985 | (8) A pre‑trial examination outside Singapore must be conducted by the examiner appointed by the Court and in the manner directed by the Court and the examiner must not do anything that is contrary to the law of that place.
@ref O 9 r 24(8) (src:985)
GIVEN `the pre-trial examination is outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is conducted by the examiner appointed by the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is conducted in the manner directed by the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 24(8) the pre-trial examination outside Singapore is conducted as required` MEANS
    IF `the pre-trial examination is outside Singapore`
    THEN
        IF `it is conducted by the examiner appointed by the Court` AND `it is conducted in the manner directed by the Court`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be conducted by the examiner appointed by the Court and in the manner directed by the Court" (a "must" not met, fork F-must in NOTES.md) [marginal-c]
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A pre-trial examination outside Singapore"; a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05, (c))

-- src:985 | (8) A pre‑trial examination outside Singapore must be conducted by the examiner appointed by the Court and in the manner directed by the Court and the examiner must not do anything that is contrary to the law of that place.
@ref O 9 r 24(8) (src:985)
GIVEN `the thing is contrary to the law of the place of the pre-trial examination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 24(8) the examiner may do the thing` MEANS
    IF `the thing is contrary to the law of the place of the pre-trial examination`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the examiner must not do anything that is contrary to the law of that place" (flat negative, ruling N2)
