-- src:991 | 25. —(1) Subject to these Rules, at the appropriate stage, the Court must give directions for the case to proceed to trial or hearing. (2) The Court may order a bifurcated hearing in that the issues concerning liability are to be heard by a Judge before the issues concerning the amount of damages or the taking of accounts are heard by a Judge or the Registrar.
@ref O 9 r 25(1) (src:991)
GIVEN `these Rules otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the appropriate stage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 25(1) the Court must give directions for the case to proceed to trial or hearing` MEANS
    IF `these Rules otherwise provide`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to these Rules"
    ELSE
        IF `it is the appropriate stage`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at the appropriate stage" [marginal-b]

-- src:991 | 25. —(1) Subject to these Rules, at the appropriate stage, the Court must give directions for the case to proceed to trial or hearing. (2) The Court may order a bifurcated hearing in that the issues concerning liability are to be heard by a Judge before the issues concerning the amount of damages or the taking of accounts are heard by a Judge or the Registrar.
@ref O 9 r 25(2) (src:991)
GIVEN `the issues concerning liability are heard by` IS A `Decision maker`
      `the issues concerning the amount of damages or the taking of accounts are heard by` IS A `Decision maker`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 25(2) the Court may order a bifurcated hearing` MEANS
    IF `the issues concerning liability are heard by` EQUALS `A Judge` AND (`the issues concerning the amount of damages or the taking of accounts are heard by` EQUALS `A Judge` OR `the issues concerning the amount of damages or the taking of accounts are heard by` EQUALS `The Registrar`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "issues concerning liability are to be heard by a Judge before the issues concerning the amount of damages or the taking of accounts are heard by a Judge or the Registrar" [marginal-b]

