DECLARE `o 9 r 25(5) a thing that may be done` IS ONE OF
    `o 9 r 25(5) the defendant sets the action down for trial`
    `o 9 r 25(5) the defendant applies to the Court to dismiss the action`
    `o 9 r 25(5) the Court orders the action to be dismissed`
    `o 9 r 25(5) the Court makes such order as the Court thinks just`

-- src:994 | (5) Where the claimant does not, within the period fixed under paragraph (4), set down the action for trial, the defendant may set the action down for trial or may apply to the Court to dismiss the action and, on the hearing of any such application, the Court may order the action to be dismissed accordingly or make such order as the Court thinks just.
@ref O 9 r 25(5) (src:994)
GIVEN `the claimant has not set down the action for trial within the period fixed under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      thing IS A `o 9 r 25(5) a thing that may be done`
      `the defendant has applied to dismiss the action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 9 r 25(5) this may be done` MEANS
    IF `the claimant has not set down the action for trial within the period fixed under paragraph (4)`
    THEN
        CONSIDER thing
        WHEN `o 9 r 25(5) the defendant sets the action down for trial` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 9 r 25(5) the defendant applies to the Court to dismiss the action` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `o 9 r 25(5) the Court orders the action to be dismissed` THEN
            IF `the defendant has applied to dismiss the action`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the hearing of any such application" [marginal-b]
        WHEN `o 9 r 25(5) the Court makes such order as the Court thinks just` THEN
            IF `the defendant has applied to dismiss the action`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the hearing of any such application" [marginal-b]
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the claimant does not, within the period fixed under paragraph (4), set down the action for trial" (a "where" that fails, ruling of 2026-11-05, (b))

